---
// About + current focus. Real, honest, no seniority inflation.
---

<section class="section" id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker" data-reveal>~/about</p>
    <h2 class="h2" data-reveal>What I build & why</h2>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-copy" data-reveal>
        <p>
          I'm an <strong>independent developer</strong> building with AI as a
          force multiplier, not a crutch: the sites here have their own design
          systems and accessibility gates, the servers have real failure
          handling, and the trading research refuses to claim performance it
          hasn't proven.
        </p>
        <p>
          My range runs from <strong>front-end motion engineering</strong>
          (GSAP, Lenis, scroll choreography) through <strong>LLM
          infrastructure</strong> (provider routing, OpenAI-compatible APIs) to
          <strong>quantitative trading tools</strong> (MQL5, backtesting,
          walk-forward validation). One builder, whole stack.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work under a <strong>zero-leak policy</strong> — every repository on
          this profile passed a Gitleaks secret scan before it was published.
          Ambitious, but honest: each project is labeled with its true status.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="focus-list" data-reveal>
        <li>
          <span class="f-label">shipping</span>
          <p>Quality House v4 — aliveness passes, Interlude page turns, scroll-driven tree rotation</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="f-label">researching</span>
          <p>SMC strategy robustness — walk-forward + real fill simulation before any live claim</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="f-label">building</span>
          <p>Free-LLM gateway — provider health checks, fallback chains, streaming correctness</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="f-label">practicing</span>
          <p>Zero-leak engineering — scanned, gated, verified git workflows</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- marquee: real project names, decorative-but-truthful rhythm -->
<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    {Array.from({ length: 2 }).map(() => (
      <>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> quality-house-v4</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> freellmapi</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> smt-lab</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> memo-smt-ea</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> mimo-vscode</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> fable5-pipeline</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> motion-lab</span>
        <span><span class="star">✦</span> gitleaks-gated</span>
      </>
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
